  "result": "I wrote the 30-minute lesson \"Context and memory in an agent\" for objective O3. A short quiz on it is ready as quiz 0002. I didn't run or open the lesson page, and I haven't looked at the quiz and key since writing them.\n\nThe lesson covers five things:\n- **The context window:** what fills it, why tokens set the cost, and why the model keeps nothing between calls.\n- **What is kept between steps:** a worked three-call bandsaw example with the input-token total, then a derivation of how that total grows with the number of steps.\n- **When the context gets too full:** context rot, compaction, clearing old tool results and sub-agents.\n- **What is kept between sessions:** saved notes, with Python code. It states plainly that a note or a student's claim never decides a booking; the training record is read by a tool at that moment.\n- **Retrieval from the manuals:** chunking, embeddings and cosine similarity, with a worked example and Python code.\n\nIt closes with a placement exercise, two cost exercises, and links to the sources it drew on.\n\nThe lesson went through two content reviews, a check against your learning preferences, a check of every reference, and a consistency edit. All findings from those were fixed.\n\nI also added a one-page cheat sheet on context and memory, updated the notes and the list of resources, and wrote a record of the review loop.\n\nAsk me for the quiz when you want it, and ask me anything about the lesson in the chat.\n\nOne question for you: do you want the quiz to cover the cost arithmetic from the lesson at the same weight as the safety rule about training records?",
